# UI / UX Design Principles

## Core Philosophy
Deliver **Apple-level polish**: intuitive, minimal, delightful, responsive.

## Visual Language
1. Use Tailwind CSS + Nuxt UI tokens; no custom CSS unless necessary.
2. **Typography**: San Francisco / Inter as default; consistent scale (Major Third).
3. Color palette: soft neutrals, Goethe brand teal accent; respect dark mode.
4. Elevation & depth via subtle shadows (2-4 dp). Blur on modal backgrounds.

## Layout & Navigation
- Main shell: top bar (brand + score), collapsible sidebar on dashboard.
- Exam mode: distraction-free, full-width, progress bar top, timer right.
- Mobile first (≥ 320 px), then enhance desktop; use CSS grid flexibly.

## Interaction
- 44 × 44 px minimum touch targets.
- Transitions: 150–250 ms ease-out; spring for card flips.
- Provide **immediate** visual feedback on selection (radio highlight).
- Keyboard shortcuts: ← → to navigate questions.
- Persist scroll & answer state on route changes (keep-alive).

## Accessibility
- All interactive elements labelled (`aria-label`, `aria-describedby`).
- Color contrast ratio ≥ 4.5.
- Focus order logical; outline visible.
- Announce score via `aria-live` region.

## Content & Copy
- Use English UI; German texts only where testing reading ability.
- Tone: encouraging, concise, no jargon.
- Error messages actionable ("Please choose an answer before continuing").

## Dashboard
- Card grid summarising latest score, average, best, streak.
- Sparkline charts via `@vueuse/chart` or lightweight canvas; no heavy libs.
- CTA buttons: "Start Full Exam", "Quick Practice".

## Exam Experience
- Part title + brief instructions atop each section.
- Disable forward navigation until current question answered (option in settings).
- Timer counts down total 30 min; warn at 5 min.

## Offline & PWA
- Encourage install banner after second visit.
- App icon: simple book motif; splash screen light & dark.

## Animation Budget
- 60fps mandatory; total JS per interaction under 2 kbms.
- Prefer CSS transitions; avoid JS-heavy animations.

## Form Elements
- Use floating labels for inputs.
- Password field masked with toggle.

## Testing
- Manual QA checklist: dark mode, RTL, keyboard only, screen reader.

*Adhere strictly to these principles to ensure a refined, inclusive user experience.*
